    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="class_driver" kindref="compound">Driver</ref> for the left and right joint encoders. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Handles initialization of both encoders and converts raw encoder counts into relative angular positions in degrees.</para>
<para>The first valid encoder position is treated as zero. Subsequent samples handle the 0–4095 rollover automatically. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>theory</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Even if there is only one possible unified theory. it is just a set of rules and equations.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Typical usage: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="class_encoder_driver_1aa47e5b6a9a2712320f3ee1ec7bcf7fec" kindref="member">EncoderDriver</ref><sp/>driver;</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">driver.<ref refid="class_encoder_driver_1a7bffef70d334fae2b32c6bf6e9fba168" kindref="member">begin</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal">EncoderPositions<sp/>positions<sp/>=<sp/>driver.<ref refid="class_encoder_driver_1aabf88a18cadbaefa3a917ba2fc68f84c" kindref="member">sample</ref>();</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
